<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4348" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atthis</span></b>  (better than <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Attis</span></b> ), ĭdis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. f.</i>, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτθίς</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Attic</i> or <i>Athenian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">matres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					11, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lingua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1</span></i>
			, praef. Oud. —Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>An Athenian woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Hippol. 107</span></i>.—Esp., <i>Philomela;</i> and, since she was changed to a nightingale, meton.
			for <i>a nightingale</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 1,
				54, 9</span></i>. Also <i>Procne</i>, <i>the sister of Philomela;</i> acc. to the fable (cf. <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet. 200</span></i>), changed into a
			swallow; hence, meton. for <i>a swallow</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 5,
			67</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A female friend of Sappho</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Non oculis grata est Atthis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					15, 18</span></i>
			 Merk. ubi v. Loers.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A name for Attica</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atthide temptantur gressus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 1116</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 5, 44</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 7,
		10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
